// For-loop over a specialized array: range() with int-literal
// arguments lowers to OvInt64Array, and the loop variable stays
// in a raw C numeric local -- no per-iteration boxing, no
// runtime arithmetic calls. Same closed-form-free arithmetic as
// intloop.ov (xor/shift defeats the affine-recurrence
// optimiser), so every implementation actually runs the loop.
// Result check: 202067735460992.
total = 0
for i in range(0, 20000000) {
    total = total + (i ^ (i >> 3)) - 1
}
print(total)
